From 8ca2d1361a3f0a36f71b7e692319b800cf5c11c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: celenity <celenity@celenity.dev>
Date: Wed, 4 Feb 2026 04:27:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: Remove OpenAI backend

Removes the OpenAI backend from Mozilla's ML (machine learning) component.

Signed-off-by: celenity <celenity@celenity.dev>

LibreWolf note: this patch is only half of the removal. It comments out every
*reference* to the OpenAI backend; the two paths themselves,

    toolkit/components/ml/content/backends/OpenAIPipeline.mjs
    toolkit/components/ml/vendor/openai/

are deleted by delete_from_tree() in scripts/librewolf-patches.py, because a
unified diff would have to carry all ~340KB of the vendored SDK to express that
- the very code this patch exists to get rid of. The jar.mn and license.html
hunks below name both paths verbatim, so an upstream rename rejects here and
`make check-patchfail` catches it. Do not relax that context: it is the
tripwire for the deletions. See landmine L4 in docs/android/AGENTS.md.

Both hunks also cover the NIGHTLY_BUILD-only reference to
vendor/openai/dist/openai-dev.mjs (jar.mn, license.html). The preprocessor
drops it on release and beta, so leaving it alone was harmless there, but a
nightly-channel build reaches it and would fail packaging on a file
delete_from_tree() has already removed. Commenting it out costs nothing on
release and extends the rename tripwire to the -dev path.

Firefox 157 desktop merge - this file is now the DESKTOP (Firefox 157) text,
listed in assets/patches/desktop.txt. Android stays on firefox-153.0esr and
keeps the text it was built and verified against, byte-identical, as
patches/android/remove-openai-esr.patch (android.txt). The two cannot share
one file: on 157, toolkit/components/ml/jar.mn lost the wllama-module-dev.mjs
line and the content/global/ml/security/* entries that the 153 text quotes as
context, so the 153 jar.mn hunk 2 rejects and hunk 1 only lands at fuzz 2.
This text was regenerated with diff -u from the real firefox-157.0 source
files, not by loosening context: jar.mn is again a single hunk at fuzz 0, every
`-` line still names an OpenAI path in full (OpenAIPipeline.mjs,
vendor/openai/dist/openai.mjs, vendor/openai/dist/openai-dev.mjs in both
jar.mn and license.html), and the set of files referencing those paths is the
same five on 157 as on 153. Fold the two back into one common.txt entry when
Android moves to an ESR >= 157.
